      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of removing yourself feels like the ultimate act of control, a final, definitive statement on your own perceived failure. But dignity isn't found in erasure; it's found in the quiet, undeniable truth of your own self-worth, even if it's messy. If you truly believe you are the stain, then the only way to prove that belief wrong is to simply *be*, right here, right now.",
